# Scheduling:
#  - Tile the inner j loop of the first MVT for better cache and
#    vectorization behavior.
#  - Parallelize its outer i loop: iterations of that loop are
#    independent (each writes a distinct x1[i] and only reads A/y_1),
#    so they can safely execute in parallel.
# The second MVT already has contiguous row access to A and a simple
# inner i loop; we leave it for the C compiler to vectorize.
